                <pb facs="0225" n="123" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg123"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/322: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">McMillin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-03-24T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 24, 1918,
                                1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.56
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>In view recent publications in Chilean and Peruvian papers on Tacna Arica dispute
                    reported by me, I discussed question with Minister of Foreign Affairs. He says
                    that nothing at all being done by two Governments concerning the question.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">McMillin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
